# 7. JavaScript loading strategy

This refactor should prioritize correctness over fashionable architecture.

The old JavaScript lives inside one IIFE and therefore currently shares one scope.

For this task, use **ordered external classic scripts with `defer`**, unless there is a compelling technical reason not to.

Example:

```html
<script defer src="js/core.js"></script>
<script defer src="js/i18n.js"></script>
...
<script defer src="js/main.js"></script>
```

All files must be loaded in explicit dependency-safe order.

Using `defer` ensures the DOM has been parsed before top-level DOM-dependent initialization occurs and keeps script execution order predictable.

Do not convert this project to ES modules merely for appearances if doing so creates a large import/export rewrite or circular dependency problem.

This is a structural extraction first.

Because the original IIFE will no longer surround all files, place:

```js
"use strict";
```

at the top of each JavaScript file.

Ensure every top-level identifier is declared exactly once.

Audit for accidental duplicate declarations after splitting.

There must be no `ReferenceError`, TDZ error, missing declaration, or ordering bug caused by the split.

If you determine that a specific browser-global name would collide after removing the IIFE, resolve that narrowly and consistently. Do not use that as a reason for a wholesale rewrite.

