# 9. Preserve execution timing

One of the biggest risks in this refactor is moving code that used to be declared before/after another declaration.

Remember:

* Function bodies can refer to functions declared later if they are not executed until later.
* Top-level expressions execute immediately.
* Top-level initializers that use constants must run after those constants exist.
* Event callbacks can safely reference later-defined functions when the callbacks do not run until after all deferred scripts have executed.
* Boot logic must run last.

Move all current immediate boot actions into `main.js` where necessary.

Do not allow a file to execute application startup halfway through loading the dependency chain.

